	<key>This deletes every slot value, the journal of edits, the context documents, the translation memory and the saved run positions — the app-side session, for every project at once.

It stays: the project list, and every .xcstrings file. A catalog keeps the strings and the translations already written into it.

What a re-scan cannot rebuild: the context documents and the translation memory are what the app LEARNED from your corrections, and this deletes them. Edits a window is still holding — anything not yet written to a file — go with the session.

Open catalogs re-read their files afterwards and read as untranslated work. The rows go in ONE pass, so even a large store is emptied in a second or two.</key>
	<string>Ka mukua e tēnei ngā uara slot katoa, te hautaka whakatikanga, ngā tuhinga horopaki, te mahara whakamaori me ngā tūnga oma kua tiakina — te wātū taha-taupānga, mō ngā kaupapa katoa i te wā kotahi.

Ka noho: te rārangi kaupapa, me ia kōnae .xcstrings. Ka pupuri te rārangi i ngā aho me ngā whakamaoritanga kua tuhia kē ki roto.

He mea kāore e taea e te karapa anō te hanga: ko ngā tuhinga horopaki me te mahara whakamaori ngā mea i AKO te taupānga mai i āu whakatikanga, ā, ka mukua e tēnei. Ngā whakatikanga e pupuri tonu ana te matapihi — ngā mea kāore anō kia tuhia ki te kōnae — ka haere tahi me te wātū.

Ka pānui anō ngā rārangi tuwhera i ō rātou kōnae i muri mai, ā, ka pānuitia hei mahi kāore anō kia whakamaoritia. Ka uru ngā rarangi i te HAERE kotahi, nō reira ahakoa he toa nui ka whakawāteahia i te hēkona kotahi, e rua rānei.</string>
